H0572.strongs:
Origin: from 4969;
Meaning: properly, something expansive, i.e. a bag
KJV renders: sack.

H0573.strongs:
Origin: from 571; veracious;
Meaning: Amittai, an Israelite
KJV renders: Amittai.

H0574.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to that of 4975;
Meaning: well-loined (i.e. burly) or mighty
KJV renders: terrible.

H0575.strongs:
Origin: or אָנָה; contracted from 370;
Meaning: where?; hence, whither?, when?; also hither and thither
KJV renders: any (no) whither, now, where, whither(-soever).

H0576.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) or אֲנָה; (Aramaic), corresponding to 589;
Meaning: I
KJV renders: I, as for me.

H0577.strongs:
Origin: or אָנָּה; apparent contracted from 160 and 4994;
Meaning: oh now!
KJV renders: I (me) beseech (pray) thee, O.

H0578.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to groan
KJV renders: lament, mourn.

H0579.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root (perhaps rather identical with 578 through the idea of contraction in anguish);
Meaning: to approach; hence, to meet in various senses
KJV renders: befall, deliver, happen, seek a quarrel.

H0580.strongs:
Origin: contracted for 587;
Meaning: we
KJV renders: we.

H0581.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) or (feminine) אִנִּיןlemma אֵנִּין first vowel, corrected to אִנִּין; (Aramaic), corresponding to 1992;
Meaning: they
KJV renders: × are, them, these.

H0582.strongs:
Origin: from 605;
Meaning: properly, a mortal (and thus differing from the more dignified 120); hence, a man in general (singly or collectively)
KJV renders: another, × (blood-) thirsty, certain, chap(-man); divers, fellow, × in the flower of their age, husband, (certain, mortal) man, people, person, servant, some (× of them), stranger, those, their trade. It is often unexpressed in the English versions, especially when used in apposition with another word. Compare 376.

H0583.strongs:
Origin: the same as 582;
Meaning: Enosh, a son of Seth
KJV renders: Enos.

H0584.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to sigh
KJV renders: groan, mourn, sigh.

H0585.strongs:
Origin: from 584;
Meaning: sighing
KJV renders: groaning, mourn, sigh.

H0586.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) or אֲנַחְנָה; (Aramaic), corresponding to 587;
Meaning: we
KJV renders: we.

H0587.strongs:
Origin: apparently from 595;
Meaning: we
KJV renders: ourselves, us, we.

H0588.strongs:
Origin: probably from the same root as 5170; a gorge or narrow pass;
Meaning: Anacharath, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Anaharath.

H0589.strongs:
Origin: contracted from 595;
Meaning: I
KJV renders: I, (as for) me, mine, myself, we, × which, × who.

H0590.strongs:
Origin: probably from 579 (in the sense of conveyance);
Meaning: a ship or (collectively) a fleet
KJV renders: galley, navy (of ships).

H0591.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 590;
Meaning: a ship
KJV renders: ship(-men).

H0592.strongs:
Origin: from 578;
Meaning: groaning
KJV renders: lamentation, sorrow.

H0593.strongs:
Origin: from 578 and 5971; groaning of (the) people;
Meaning: Aniam, an Israelite
KJV renders: Aniam.

H0594.strongs:
Origin: probably from an unused root meaning to be narrow;
Meaning: according to most a plumb-line, and to others a hook
KJV renders: plumb-line

H0595.strongs:
Origin: sometimes, אָנֹכִי; a primitive pronoun;
Meaning: I
KJV renders: I, me, × which.

H0596.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to mourn, i.e. complain
KJV renders: complain.

H0598.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 597;
Meaning: figuratively, to distress
KJV renders: trouble.

H0599.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to breathe hard, i.e. be enraged
KJV renders: be angry (displeased).
